  #sol-item(1, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Disaster is exposure plus vulnerability, not magnitude alone.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Floods, droughts, storms and earthquakes are natural hazards.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    It is land losing its cover and productivity, usually through overuse and drought.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The cover is stripped by too many animals and too much wood cutting.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    It runs from Senegal to Djibouti, with eleven Nigerian states involved.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Wood fuel, land clearing and timber remove the forest faster than it regrows.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Bare soil is washed away, and less water soaks in to recharge the ground.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Sheet erosion strips the fertile surface film; gullies are its later stage.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Steep slopes, heavy rain and cleared cover concentrate runoff into gullies.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Where the cover is thin and the soil is dry, the wind lifts the fines.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Steps cut the slope length, so the water arrives slowly.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Ploughing across the slope traps water in the furrows.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Trees hold the soil, shade it and slow the wind.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Traffic, private generators and flares are the sources the paper names.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Spills and untreated discharges poison the creeks and the fishing grounds.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Rain washes the waste into the water table and the wells.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Lead, mercury and cadmium in old electronics poison the dump sites.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Conservation manages use so the resource renews; preservation leaves it untouched.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Yankari, Cross River and Gashaka-Gumti are the Nigerian examples.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The Brundtland definition balances present needs against future capacity.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The three must overlap; running one alone costs the other two.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The Sahel is drying, the coast is flooding, and the rains are less predictable.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Both are climate agreements, with different obligations for rich and poor states.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The country suffers the effects while contributing little to the cause.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The MDGs ran to 2015, when the seventeen SDGs were adopted.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Goal 13 is climate action; goal 6 is water and goal 15 is life on land.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Exposure and drainage decide the damage, not the rainfall total alone.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Drains and planning keep the water out of the houses.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    A warning cannot stop a flood, but it can empty the street.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Waves, sand mining and harbour works all eat the shoreline.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Afforestation establishes new cover; reforestation restores an old one.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Different crops take different nutrients, and the rotation starves the pests.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The cover holds moisture, cools the soil and stops the rain from beating it.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "A", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    Solar, wind, hydro and biomass renew; the fossil fuels do not.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "B", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
    The gas could generate electricity or be exported as LNG.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "D", dense: true, pad: 10.0pt)[
